    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="99487d4b-3f5d-545c-8ac3-692318b31241" activityNameId="00c094ed-1b94-5e78-aa0d-058572f18549" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Hot rolling, electric steel</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Hot rolling, electric steel
This process was created based on the following process: "Hot rolling, steel {RER}". The material input for the loss consists of 100% secondary material. The ‘sheet rolling, electric’ process with secondary material was used to have only secondary material flows in the upstream process chain. 

To achieve greater toughness, shock resistance and tensile strength, the raw steel production outputs cast ingots, slabs, billets and beam blanks are hot rolled to long or flat products or semifinished products.

Synonyms: Hot forming 
UUID: 79322981-a6cf-47f1-8918-69b7be9f4f20
Location: Data relate to plants in Europe
Technology: Average technique for EU. Assumption: heating 100% with natural gas. Furnaces of about 10 MW are approxi-mated by furnace "&gt; 100 kW"
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: Data from literature
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_79322981-a6cf-47f1-8918-69b7be9f4f20.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
